  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposal, due to its two-storey nature, close proximity to the shared boundary with No. 79 Welbeck Road and position to the south west of the rear windows and rear garden of this property, and without evidence to the contrary, would adversely affect the amenity of 79 Welbeck Road in terms of loss of light. As such, the proposal is contrary to Policy 29 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018.",
    "The proposed two-storey side extension, by reason of its excessive width, scale and proximity to the side boundary, would appear out of keeping with the host dwelling and surrounding area. It would fail to respect the prevailing pattern of development, which is characterised by wide gaps to the sides of end-of-terrace properties at the Whitland Road/Welbeck Road junction. The development would dominate the host building and result in an overdevelopment of this constrained and prominent corner site, creating a cramped and incongruous form of development that harms the openness of the site and the character of the area. As such, the proposal is contrary to Policy 28 of the Sutton Local Plan 2018 and the guidance set out in Supplementary Planning Documents SPD4 'Design of Residential Extensions' and SPD14 'Creating Locally Distinctive Places'."
  ],
